speechtext:
1.	How	many	permanent	civil	servants	areemployed in each of the following annual salary brackets: (a) less than $1,860; (b) $1,860 to $2,240; (c)	over $2,240	to	$2,480;	(d)	over	$2,480	to	$2,780;(e)	over $2,780	to	$3,130;	(f)	over	$3,130	to	$3,480;(g)	over $3,480	to	$3,830;	(h)	over	$3,830	to	$4,860;
(i) over $4,860 to $6,860; (j) over $6,860?
2.	How	many	temporary	civil	servants	areemployed in each of the following annual salary brackets: (a) less than $1,860; (b) $1,860 to $2,240; (c)	over $2,240	to	$2,480;	(d)	over	$2,480	to	$2,780;(e)	over $2,780	to	$3,130;	(f)	over	$3,130	to	$3,480;(g)	over $3,480	to	$3,830;	(h)	over	$3,830	to	$4,860;
(i) over $4,860 to $6,860; (j) over $6,860?
3.	How	many	seasonal	civil	servants	areemployed in each of the following salary brackets: (a) less than $1,860; (b) $1,860 to $2,240; (c)	over $2,240	to	$2,480;	(d)	over	$2,480	to	$2,780;(e)	over $2,780	to	$3,130;	(f)	over	$3,130	to	$3,480;(g)	over $3,480	to	$3,830;	(h)	over	$3,830	to	$4,860;
(i) over $4,860 to $6,860; (j) over $6,860?
